{# W3C SCXML 4.7: Log action

   An author's label is an ARGUMENT to Printf, never part of its format
   string. `fmt` reads `%` as a verb, so a label reading `percent %s here`
   spliced into the format string is a verb with no argument behind it and
   `go vet` fails the build — measured 2026-09-14. Escaping cannot fix that:
   `\%` is not how Printf escapes a percent, and the value was never wrong,
   its POSITION was. `generator::register_template` escapes it for the
   literal it sits in (`literal_text`), which is the other half.

   The default is hoisted once rather than restated at each of the three
   sites below, so the three cannot drift apart. #}
{%- set label = action.label | default('') -%}
{% if action.expr and model.needs_script_engine %}
	{
		logResult, logErr := p.ScriptEngine.EvaluateExpression(p.SessionID, `{{ action.expr | to_lua_expr }}`)
		if logErr == nil {
			fmt.Printf("%s%v\n", "{{ label }}", logResult)
		}
	}
{% elif action.expr %}
	fmt.Println("{{ label }}{{ action.expr | escape_go }}")
{% else %}
	fmt.Println("{{ label }}")
{% endif %}
